>> title: Chettinad Chicken Chukka
>> description: Chettinad Chicken Chukka with bold, roasted flavours!
>> course: 
>> author: 
>> source: 
>> time required: 
>> image: 
>> servings: 

== For the spice mix ==

Heat a #kadhai{} and dry roast @Kashmiri red chillies{8}, @coriander seeds{1%tbsp}, @fennel seeds{1%tbsp}, @cinnamon{1%inch}, @green cardamoms{4} and @curry leaves{1%sprig}.

Add @cashew nuts{2%tbsp} and @roasted chana dal{2%tbsp} and roast again. Finally add @fresh grated coconut{1/2%cup} and roast till it turns golden brown.

Cool completely and grind into a fine powder.

== For the chicken ==

Heat @sesame oil{1/4%cup} in a #kadhai{}. Add @curry leaves{1%sprig} and @shallots{1/2%cup}.

Sauté till the shallots turn golden brown.

Add @ginger paste{1%tbsp} and @garlic paste{1%tbsp} and cook for ~{1%minute}.

Add the @chicken{1%kg} and sauté on a high flame for ~{5%minutes}.

Add @turmeric powder{1/4%tsp}, the prepared spice powder and @sesame oil{1%tbsp}. Mix well on a medium flame.

Add @salt{}(to taste) and @water{1/2%cup}. Cover and cook till the chicken is done and the oil starts separating.

Once the oil separates, remove the lid and continue sautéing till all the moisture evaporates and the masala coats the chicken beautifully.

Finish with @lemon juice{1/2%lemon}(juice of) and @fresh coriander{2%tbsp}(chopped). Mix once and serve hot.
